  "sections": [
    {
      "block_id": "h1-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Validation Scheduler",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Overview",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The Validation Scheduler is a Phase 0 control-plane system built into the Validate tool. It owns three responsibilities that parallel agents cannot reliably manage themselves: **caching**, **request coalescing**, and **bounded parallelism**.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Agents do not choose wrappers, remember to check for running validations, or coordinate xdist flags. The Validate tool owns this.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Cache",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "How it works",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. Before running a check, Validate computes an `input_fingerprint` from: - Normalized command fingerprint - `pyproject.toml` content hash (if present) - `uv.lock` content hash (if present) - `pytest.ini` / `setup.cfg` / `tox.ini` content hashes - `docs/schemas/*` file hashes (for `schema`-kind checks) - Python version - Tool versions (pytest, ruff, pyright) — hashed from `--version` output - Current working directory",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "2. A `cache_key` is derived from check identity + command fingerprint + input fingerprint + cwd.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "3. The cache store is file-backed under `.build/rig/validation-cache/records/<prefix>/<key>.json`.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-10",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Cache invalidation",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A cache entry is invalidated when: - The command fingerprint changes (different args) - Any input file changes (pyproject.toml, uv.lock, pytest config, schemas) - Python version changes - Tool version changes - The cache record is corrupt (JSON parse failure) - `cache_policy=force_rerun` is set",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Reuse policy",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- **Passed results**: reused by default (`cache_status=\"hit\"`) - **Failed results**: written to cache but NOT reused unless `allow_failed_cache_reuse=true` - **Corrupt records**: treated as miss, rerun occurs - **`cache_policy=disabled`**: bypasses cache entirely - **`cache_policy=force_rerun`**: bypasses cache, forces re-execution",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-14",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Scheduler / Coalescing",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-15",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Running lock",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Each cache key has a file-based running lock under `.build/rig/validation-scheduler/locks/`.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- If a check with the same cache key is already running (`lock_running_checks=true`), the duplicate gets `scheduler_status=\"blocked_duplicate\"` and does NOT execute. - Locks expire after 5 minutes without heartbeat (stale detection). - Stale locks are cleaned up on next scheduler operation.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-18",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Behavior",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "code-19",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Check A starts → lock acquired for cache_key X\nCheck B requested same X → lock active → B gets blocked_duplicate\nCheck A finishes → lock released\nCheck C requested X → lock free → runs normally",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "detailed",
        "collapsible": true,
        "collapsed_by_default": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-20",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Phase 0 limitation",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Following/waiting for in-flight checks is deferred. The requesting agent sees `blocked_duplicate` status and should retry later if needed.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-22",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Bounded Parallelism",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-23",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Policy",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Validate rewrites pytest commands to inject bounded xdist flags:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-25",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Condition",
        "Behavior"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Cache hit",
          "No injection (no run occurs)"
        ],
        [
          "Not pytest",
          "Not applicable"
        ],
        [
          "Already has `-n`",
          "Not applicable (respects existing)"
        ],
        [
          "Focused single file",
          "Stays serial unless `parallel_policy=force`"
        ],
        [
          "Schema validation",
          "Stays serial"
        ],
        [
          "ruff/pyright",
          "Stays serial"
        ],
        [
          "xdist unavailable",
          "Falls back to serial, warning emitted"
        ],
        [
          "Default",
          "Injects `-n <workers> --dist <mode>`"
        ]
      ],
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-26",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Worker limits",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Default max workers: `min(4, os.cpu_count() or 1)` - Configurable via `max_workers` - Never `-n auto` by default — always bounded",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-28",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Why not `-n auto`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "`-n auto` uses all CPU cores, which melts laptops during parallel agent activity. Bounded workers keep the machine usable.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-30",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Validation Phases",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-31",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Phase",
        "Behavior"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "`edit`",
          "Full-suite validation emits `full_suite_during_edit_phase` warning. Cache still works normally."
        ],
        [
          "`pre_report`",
          "Normal validation. No phase warnings."
        ],
        [
          "`cleanup`",
          "Normal validation with cache."
        ],
        [
          "`final`",
          "Normal validation with cache."
        ]
      ],
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-32",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Phases emit **warnings only** — never hard failures.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-33",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Content-Light Records",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-34",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Cache records contain: - `status`, `exit_code`, `duration_ms` - `stdout_sha256`, `stderr_sha256` - `stdout_bytes`, `stderr_bytes` - `failure_kind` - `cache_key`, `input_fingerprint`, `input_file_fingerprints` - `validation_phase`, `worker_count`, `distribution` - `warnings`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Cache records do NOT contain: - Raw `stdout` / `stderr` content - File diffs or patches - Prompts or secrets - Full raw `argv` (only fingerprint)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-36",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "End-to-End Integration",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "ValidateTool.run() directly owns cache and scheduler behavior — agents do not opt in:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. Every `run()` call creates `ValidationCacheStore` and `ValidationSchedulerStore` from args. 2. For each check, the tool computes `input_fingerprint` and `cache_key`, looks up cache, and checks eligibility. 3. Cache hits return `_build_cached_result()` with `cache_status=\"hit\"` and the stored record's metadata. 4. Cache misses run the check, store the result, and annotate the check with `cache_status=\"miss_ran\"`. 5. Scheduler acquires a file-based lock before running; duplicate cache keys get `scheduler_status=\"blocked_duplicate\"`. 6. `apply_parallel_policy()` injects bounded xdist flags for eligible pytest commands. 7. `check_lifecycle_policy()` emits `full_suite_during_edit_phase` warnings when appropriate. 8. On cache/scheduler errors, the tool falls through to the real check — never crashes.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-39",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Test coverage (216 tests passing)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-40",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "End-to-end tests through `ValidateTool.run()` prove:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-41",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Test",
        "What it proves"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "`test_run_end_to_end_cache_hit`",
          "First run executes; second identical call returns cached result with `cache_status=\"hit\"`"
        ],
        [
          "`test_run_end_to_end_cache_miss_on_invalidation`",
          "Unrelated file changes don't invalidate; scope-based invalidation requires fingerprint change"
        ],
        [
          "`test_run_end_to_end_cache_content_light`",
          "Result has no raw stdout/stderr in JSON dump; cache metadata always present"
        ],
        [
          "`test_run_end_to_end_cache_disabled_produces_no_cache`",
          "`cache_policy=disabled` skips cache entirely, all checks show `cache_status=\"disabled\"`"
        ],
        [
          "`test_run_end_to_end_force_rerun_ignores_cache`",
          "`cache_policy=force_rerun` bypasses cache, re-runs check"
        ],
        [
          "`test_run_end_to_end_scheduler_disabled_no_block`",
          "`scheduler_policy=disabled` does not acquire locks"
        ],
        [
          "`test_run_end_to_end_cache_error_resilient`",
          "Corrupt cache JSON doesn't crash — falls through to real check with `cache_status!=\"hit\"`"
        ],
        [
          "`test_run_end_to_end_cache_on_profile_with_focused_test`",
          "Path-scoped validation still caches properly"
        ]
      ],
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-42",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Pre-existing bug fix",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-43",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "`check_missing_dependency()` previously checked every non-flag token as a potential binary, which broke multi-word commands like `git status --short` (would check `status` as a binary). Fixed to only check the first resolvable binary token.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-44",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Phase 0 Limitations",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-45",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- No full coverage dependency graph - No pytest-testmon integration - No remote cache - No wait/follow for in-flight checks (deferred) - No cross-machine cache - No heartbeat renewal on running locks - No `$HOME/.rig/relay` writes — cache is project-local under `.build/rig/` - Schema validation stays serial even with `parallel_policy=auto`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-46",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Configuration",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
